{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The reference’s key numerical detail is that both outputs derive from the same float32 masked-sigmoid gradient; only `grad_dt` is rounded to bfloat16 before return, while the bias reduction sums the unrounded float32 values. I’m putting down a fused gradient/partial-reduction kernel plus a small final reduction now."}}
