{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The head-split experiment reveals a useful size-dependent tradeoff: narrow head tiles win for medium tensors by avoiding padded sigmoid work, while 64-head coalesced tiles remain best for the largest cases. Before locking dispatch thresholds, I’m optimizing the second launch itself by reducing the partials in contiguous head tiles instead of 40 separate strided programs."}}
