{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining hot operation is sigmoid: the current kernel pays for both an exponential and a reciprocal on every element, even though only the clamp-passing gradients matter. I’m evaluating a high-accuracy Padé sigmoid (one reciprocal plus fused multiplies) against the exact bfloat16 outputs and bias sums; if it stays within the workload tolerances, it should lower the compute-bound large-case time."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch\nfor n in (131072, 91072, 19984, 1172):\n  go=torch.randn((1,n,40),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16).float()\n  x=torch.randn((1,n,40),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16).float()\n  a=torch.randn((1,n,40),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16).float()\n  mask=(a>.001)&(a<.1)\n  exact=torch.where(mask,go*torch.sigmoid(x),0.)\n  z=x*.5; z2=z*z\n  pade5=.5+.5*(z*(945.+z2*(105.+z2))/(945.+z2*(420.+15.*z2)))\n  pade3=.5+.5*(z*(15.+z2)/(15.+6.*z2))\n  for name,s in (('pade5',pade5),('pade3',pade3)):\n    appr=torch.where(mask,go*s,0.)\n    e_bf=exact.bfloat16().float(); a_bf=appr.bfloat16().float()\n    diff=(e_bf-a_bf).abs(); allowed=.0012+.0078125*e_bf.abs()\n    ratio=(diff<=allowed).float().mean().item()\n    active_ratio=(diff[mask]<=allowed[mask]).float().mean().item()\n    eb=exact.sum((0,1)).bfloat16().float(); ab=appr.sum((0,1)).bfloat16().float()\n    bdiff=(eb-ab).abs(); ballow=.0012+.0078125*eb.abs()\n    print(n,name,'all',ratio,'active',active_ratio,'max',diff.max().item(),'bias_bad',int((bdiff>ballow).sum()),'bias_max',bdiff.max().item())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
