{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"Summing the rounded output is not accurate enough for the 40 bias values, so that flat-pass design is ruled out. A better exact approach is to keep one row-block program but process heads as sequential 32- and 8-wide tensors. That preserves contiguous access and float32 partial sums while eliminating the 24 padded sigmoid lanes and reducing live registers."}}
