{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The sequential 32+8 kernel is exact at the element level and materially faster on large tensors (about 20.1 µs versus ~24 µs locally). I’m testing an 8×5 sequential variant next; smaller live tiles may raise occupancy further while still covering exactly 40 heads with one row-block program."}}
